 "intro": "Forum Gallorum on the Via Aemilia, near Mutina in northern Italy, April 43 BC. Caesar has been murdered. Mark Antony is besieging Decimus Brutus in Mutina. You are the consul Gaius Vibius Pansa, bringing new legions; the other consul, Hirtius, and young Octavian are nearby.",
 "debrief": "In Appian’s account and a letter by an officer who was there, Antony ambushed Pansa’s march in the marshes near Forum Gallorum. The Martian Legion fought fiercely, but Antony won and Pansa was mortally wounded. As Antony’s tired men returned, Hirtius fell on them and routed them, so that Antony won and lost on the same day. A week later Hirtius broke Antony’s lines at Mutina but was killed; Pansa died of his wounds. Antony escaped to Gaul, and Octavian soon joined him against the Senate. The other choices are what-ifs.",
